  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Explain the difference between continuous integration, continuous delivery and continuous deployment. (6 marks)', 'Continuous integration (CI): developers merge small code changes into the shared repository several times a day; every merge automatically triggers a build and automated tests, so integration errors are found early. Continuous delivery (CD): extends CI so that every change that passes the pipeline is automatically prepared and tested in staging and is always ready to release; the actual release to production is a manual business decision (one click). Continuous deployment: goes one step further: every change that passes all automated tests is deployed to production automatically, with no human approval. So CI is about building and testing, continuous delivery keeps software releasable, and continuous deployment releases automatically.', null, '[{"point": "Continuous integration: developers merge code often into a shared repository; each commit triggers automated build and tests", "marks": 2}, {"point": "Continuous delivery: CI plus automated release pipeline; code is always deployable but release to production needs manual approval", "marks": 2}, {"point": "Continuous deployment: every change that passes tests is released to production automatically, no manual step; example/diagram of the pipeline", "marks": 2}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge') and t.slug = 'ict-general-subject-knowledge'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-2'), 'standard', 6,
